# SouqIQ — Agent-owned workflow

The project owner speaks Kurdish (Sorani) and does **not** want to run git/npm/env commands themselves. The agent must do the work.

## When the user asks (any similar phrasing)

| User intent (examples) | Agent action |
|---|---|
| Repo link / “بێنە” / clone / setup on new PC | `git clone` (or open existing folder), `npm install`, create `.env` via `npx vercel env pull .env --yes` if linked, else copy from `.env.example` and fill from Vercel/project secrets; set `AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000` for local; `npm run dev` if they want to run |
| “پوش” / push / send to GitHub | `git status`, `git diff`, commit if needed (ask only if message unclear), `git push` |
| “کۆتا ڤێرژن” / pull / sync from GitHub | `git pull`, then `npm install` if lockfile changed |
| Deploy / Vercel | Prefer GitHub push (auto-deploy). Use `npx vercel --prod` only if needed |

## Rules

- Never tell the user to “run these commands yourself” as the primary path — execute them.
- Never commit `.env` or secrets.
- Repo: `https://github.com/amd47amd/souqiq.git`
- Live site: `https://souqiq.vercel.app`
- Prefer committing and pushing when the user clearly wants changes on GitHub/Vercel.
- On a brand-new machine: if GitHub/Vercel CLI auth is missing, guide **one** login step (`gh auth login` / `vercel login`), then continue the rest yourself.
